{% doc %}
  Sends the agent back where they came from.

  Include it, do not call it as a function: it ends the response, and that
  only propagates through include.

  Why not modules/core/helpers/redirect_to: that helper publishes a flash
  of its own on the way out, every time, even when given no message. It
  writes the core {error, notice, info} shape over the same session key
  any flash set earlier in the request used, so the message the agent was
  supposed to read is replaced by an empty one and never appears. This is
  the upstream issue written up in docs/for-platformos-engineers.

  Keeps the one thing that helper does that matters here: a return path
  that is not a path on this site is refused, so a crafted form field
  cannot turn an action into an open redirect.

  @param {string} [url] - Where to go. Defaults to the queue
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign target = url | default: '/admin/support'

  assign leading = target | slice: 0, 1
  assign protocol_relative = target | slice: 0, 2

  if leading != '/' or protocol_relative == '//'
    assign target = '/admin/support'
  endif

  redirect_to target
  break
%}
